Title: World Superbikes: Toprak Razgatlioglu moves into championship lead with Donington Park treble
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [], 'Description': [{'Description': 'Toprak Razgatlioglu moved into the lead of the World Superbike Championship by winning the second feature race at Donington Park.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 97}}, {'Description': 'BMW rider Razgatlioglu had earlier closed to within one point of title rival Nicolo Bulega by winning the Superpole sprint race ahead of the Ducati rider.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 137}}, {'Description': "With his dominant victory in Sunday's feature race, reigning champion Razgatlioglu now leads the championship by four points ahead of Bulega, who was second.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 152}}, {'Description': 'Alvaro Bautista completed the podium ahead of Danilo Petrucci and Andrea Locatelli.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 77}}, {'Description': "Northern Ireland's six-time champion Jonathan Rea, who collected his best finish of the season in fifth on Saturday, claimed the final point on offer in 15th place.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 151}}, {'Description': "Sunday's win was a third victory of the weekend for the Turkish rider after he won Saturday's opening feature race and the Superpole.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 120}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Toprak Razgatlioglu '}]}
